## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of consent-driven data minimization, offline safety, and the relationship between consent lifecycle and CCA score calculation.

## Key Concepts
- Consent tokens gate data exposure
- policy_version controls exposure granularity
- Idempotent, offline-safe compute operations
- Per-user data retention settings

## Code Example
```javascript
async function computeCCA(userIdMasked, consentToken, policyVersion) {
  const consent = await consentStore.validate(consentToken, policyVersion);
  if (!consent?.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Not authorized');
  }
  const score = await calculateScore(userIdMasked, consent);
  return { user_id_masked: userIdMasked, cca_score: score };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to add A/B rollout gating to privacy-preserving analytics, determinism, offline behavior, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Deterministic variant assignment from masked ID and locale
- Privacy: no exposure of raw IDs
- Offline handling and rollback
- Observability and tests

```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function selectVariant(userIdMasked, locale, salt) {
  const data = userIdMasked + '|' + locale + '|' + salt;
  const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(data).digest('hex');
  return (parseInt(hash.substring(0,8), 16) % 2) ? 'v2' : 'v1';
}
```

